learnings:
  - Dogfooding found two bugs that had always been there (the helper line, GUI row shape) and that fakes hid. Real-kernel e2e tests are now required for GUI flows.
  - '`gnomon trace` paid off at once: it showed the sessions worked and only the GUI was broken.'
  - Aegis blocked security-relevant designs twice (in-project traces, auto-edits symlinks). Review before merge is worth it.
